[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: "BEFORE" and "AFTER" images of a character, showing a black and white version and a colored version.
AUDIO: 'Ever used a LoRA that killed your colors or style every time you used it? Don\'t give up on it. Instead, you can use this method right here so that your LoRA works how you want without needing to lower its strength. Let me explain. I\'ve seen most people use LoRAs like this.'

[00:12] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'Just connect the LoRA right into the model and that\'s about it. And that works well most of the time, but it only lets you control how much the LoRA affects the image. We also want to control when it affects it. And you can'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use it with prompts, too. I\'m going to show you at the end. For this case, I\'m going to use a slider LoRA I just trained. As sliders go, the higher that I put this at, the more extreme the pose my character will be at. So, this is'

[00:37] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing nodes for "Load Diffusion Model," "Load LORA," "CLIP Text Encode," and "KSampler," with an anime-style image result.
AUDIO: 'one. This is three. To achieve a pose I like, I need to use a very high strength. And you can see that this is cooking my image. I\'m losing the original style this had. Usually, you could fix this by just lowering the value of the LoRA. But this means that'

[00:50] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface with "Create Hook Keyframe" nodes, "Load LORA," and "KSampler" visible, showing the node connections.
AUDIO: 'you\'re sacrificing what it achieves. And as you can see, my pose is gone. So, that is where the Create Hook nodes come in. And these are native in ComfyUI, by the way. By loading the LoRA through'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'them, I can not only control the strength I\'m using it, but I can also control in what steps my LoRA is affecting the image. If I run this as a test with a fixed seed, you can see that the pose is pretty similar, but now I'

[01:14] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface comparing "lora scheduling" and "normal lora" setups, with an anime character image on the right.
AUDIO: 'still [music] keep the style that I wanted. So, how did I do this? As you can see here, my LoRA is at strength four. But here, I can also put it at strength four. However, now we go to this node. This is a scheduler node.'

[01:27] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Close-up of ComfyUI nodes, specifically "Create Hook Keyframe" with "strength_mult" and "start_percent" parameters.
AUDIO: 'It\'s giving AI instructions about two things. The first is strength multiplier, and the second one is start percentage. Strength multiplier is how strong it\'s acting. So, one would be one multiplied by four, which is four. If I'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'put it at two, it would be eight. And then the start percent is the percentage at which this action starts. Meaning, when the LoRA gets multiplied by this number. Now it\'s at 0%, so it will be at four strength. In this case, at the very'

[01:54] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "Create Hook Keyframe" nodes connected, with an anime character image result.
AUDIO: 'start, this LoRA is in full action. But then our next instruction comes in, which is multiply the strength of the Laura by zero once you\'ve done 15% of the generation. The translation of this is that this Laura will be active at'

[02:07] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "KSampler" node details (steps, cfg, sampler_name) and a blurred intermediate image.
AUDIO: 'full strength and once it reaches 15% of the total denoising, it will get multiplied by zero, therefore disappearing for the rest of the generation. And the reason why we do that is because we think that by that'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'point AI has already decided the big shapes and now it doesn\'t need that Laura anymore. In this case, you can see the sides the pose very quickly. So we can take it out early. In other examples like this one, I had to stop the Laura'

[02:31] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface with multiple "Create Hook Keyframe" nodes and "Cond Pair Set Props" connected to a "KSampler."
AUDIO: 'at 42% because if I take this earlier, you\'re going to see that the hand gets lost. What I\'m showing here is not exactly how it works, but it\'s a nice way to visualize it. And you can see that here I have a Laura in reverse. It starts deactivated and then I activated'

[02:44] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'after 20% of total steps. And the reason why is because I mainly want this Laura for style. If I take this off and I generate with this Laura from the beginning, you can see it\'s changing my pose way too much because Laura\'s will give you things that you want in the'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image as well as secondary effects that you didn\'t really ask for. So controlling the time you use them in allows you to get that effect that you wanted without needing to deal with so many little extra things that you might not want. Like here, when I\'m using this'

[03:12] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing a complex "PROMPT SCHEDULE" section with multiple text input nodes and an image of a winged character.
AUDIO: 'Laura, which is supposed to only change light, but here I have it at zero and you can see it changed the whole image I had. When it should have done something like this, which is basically changing only the lighting of the image. And this doesn\'t end at Laura\'s. Prompts have'

[03:25] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface focusing on "PROMPT SCHEDULE" nodes, specifically "PROMPT A 0.00-0.15" and "RANGE A 0.00-0.15."
AUDIO: 'exactly the same issue. This right here is an image I generated using four prompts and each one of them acted at a different time for a different reason. The idea is to keep the same general prompt but taking out and adding different parts in different times. I\'ll'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you how to do it here. First I have this prompt and since I don\'t have like strength to touch, you only have when this prompt starts and when this prompt ends. Then we have the second prompt and the only difference between these two is'

[03:52] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "RANGE A 0.00-0.15," "RANGE B 0.15-0.20," and "COMBINE A+B" nodes.
AUDIO: 'that I have first analog horror here, and then it goes away, so that it doesn\'t generate random stuff, which gives us this. And make sure that you don\'t leave prompts hanging like I did here. When it ends at 50% and then that\'s it, because it will explode. So,'

[04:05] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "KSampler" and "Save Image" nodes, with an anime character holding scythes in a dark environment.
AUDIO: 'you always have to make sure that they all add up at one. And then the next change comes. Here we are using the prompt Grim Reaper horror. And now I\'m going to change it to mid outfit, pink hair, pink eyes. After this change, we'

[04:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'get the exact same composition, but with the woman we wanted. The outfit got lost a bit, but who cares. And only after 60% of the generation has completed, I will add light particles and bright sparks.'

[04:29] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing a "PROMPT (unscheduled)" node and several generated image previews.
AUDIO: 'If I added them in the beginning, it would be way too noticeable. But I wanted is something subtle like so. And here you can see what we would have gotten if I didn\'t edit the prompt in the meantime, and just prompted directly for what I needed. And this is what we'

[04:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "PROMPT A 0.00-0.15" and "PROMPT B 0.15-0.20" nodes with their respective "RANGE" and "COMBINE" nodes.
AUDIO: 'would have gotten, and this is what we got, which is much closer to what I wanted. But Anima, this is also pretty cool to do with artist styles. For example, I really like Rob style compositions, but the rendering with Anima, I\'m not quite a fan of. So, here'

[04:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I have the composition using Rob in the prompt, and now I\'m going to change it at half the generation steps for a different artist. So, what I\'m going to get is this same composition in this idea, but with a completely different'

[05:07] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "normal lora" and "lora scheduling" sections, with an anime character image.
AUDIO: 'style that I think fits better. So, yeah. Start controlling when you add stuff in the image, and not only what or how. So, I left the boring part on how to connect this for the end, but basically, you will have to load the LoRA through a this different node'

[05:21] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "Create Hook LoRA (MO)" and "Set Hook Keyframes" nodes, with an anime character image.
AUDIO: 'instead of the normal one, and then you\'ll have to create the hook keyframes with this nodes. You connect this to set hook keyframes, and then you will have to connect this to this node. And the main change here is that instead of connecting the LoRA like usual through'

[05:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the model, you will be connecting it through the prompt. Right? So, the prompt needs to go through this node, and then this node only connects to positive and negative, and this is the node that applies the conditioning. Also, you have this, which is LoRA'

[05:45] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing "Prompt Scheduling" nodes with "PROMPT A" and "PROMPT B" and an image of a winged character on a battlefield.
AUDIO: 'scheduling, but different. If this is a substitute for the create hook key frames, it basically creates [music] them interpolated, so you just have to use one node, but it\'s going to go in a line. And for prompting, it\'s very simple. It\'s just connecting the ranges'

[05:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to this node, and then when you want to add another one, you don\'t connect it from any of these nodes, you connect it from the combination of both, right? So, you connect this one to here, and then this will have the next one, and the'

[06:09] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing a complex "PROMPT SCHEDULE" setup with multiple "COMBINE" nodes and an image of an anime character.
AUDIO: 'next one will get combined to this node and not this one. And then it goes all in the positive. If you want to look for negative, go ahead. And if you have four, the only change is that instead of this combined node going to the positive in the K sampler, it will go into the positive for this node. And that\'s'

[06:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pretty much it. I will leave the workflows in the description for you so that you can play around with them if you want. Thanks for watching. See you.'
